# route map: a dozen junctions, made up to follow a search by hand.
# This course's own (no OpenStreetMap data in it), under the repository's licence.
#
# Three rows of junctions: 0 and 1 in the south (y 0); 2 to 8 along a main
# street in the middle (y 300), 200 metres a road from 3 to 8, so 1000
# metres in five roads; 9, 10 and 11 in the north (y 600). A ring road joins
# 3 to 8 through junction 1 in two roads, but 1200 metres: the fewest
# junctions are not the fewest metres. Going from 3 to 8, Dijkstra finishes
# the streets west and north of 3 as well; A* need not.
